# CLAUDE.md — app/Providers (the explicit-registration hub)

Almost nothing is auto-discovered, and **a missing registration fails silently**. Every list here is an inventory;
check it by running the flow end to end.

## What gets registered here

- **Contract → implementation bindings** (`app/Contracts/`). An unbound contract fails at runtime, so a new contract
  gets its binding in the same commit.
- **`Gate::policy()`** for every policy, in `AppServiceProvider::boot()` (`app/Policies/CLAUDE.md`).
- **`Event::listen` wiring**, the only event → listener registry (discovery is off in `bootstrap/app.php`). A
  listener without a line never fires.
- **Observers** with `Model::observe()` in `boot()`.
<!-- if:htmx -->
- **`FortifyServiceProvider`**: the auth actions (`app/Actions/Fortify/`), the auth limiters (below), the mailed
  reset-link URL while the views are off (`routes/CLAUDE.md`), and `Fortify::viewPrefix('auth.')` once the auth pages
  exist (`resources/CLAUDE.md`, Auth pages).
<!-- endif -->
<!-- if:spa -->
- **`FortifyServiceProvider`**: the auth actions (`app/Actions/Fortify/`), the auth limiters (below),
  `ResetPassword::createUrlUsing` + `VerifyEmail::createUrlUsing` at the SvelteKit paths (`routes/CLAUDE.md`), and the
  bindings of the exported `app/Requests/Auth/` classes over Fortify's own requests (`app/Requests/CLAUDE.md`).
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:htmx -->
<!-- unless:spa -->
- **`FortifyServiceProvider`**: the auth actions (`app/Actions/Fortify/`), the auth limiters (below) and the mailed
  reset-link URL. Fortify is headless (`config/fortify.php` `views => false`, `routes/CLAUDE.md`).
<!-- endif -->
<!-- endif -->
  `Passkeys::authorizeLoginUsing()` or a `PasskeyLoginResponse` binding lives here when used (root `CLAUDE.md`, Auth).
- **`HorizonServiceProvider::gate()`**: who may see `/horizon`.
  - A **verified** email in `config('auth.admins')` (`ADMIN_EMAILS`) until roles exist: registration is open, so a
    bare email match lets anyone claim an admin's address. An unverified admin account never opens it (remedy:
    `database/CLAUDE.md`, `ProductionSeeder`).
  - `authorization()` replaces Horizon's "anyone when local" with "anyone when local **and** from the host itself"
    (loopback, or the container's default gateway). `comesFromHost` is safe only while the published web port is
    IPv4-only.
  - `WEB_BIND` / `SIDECAR_BIND` decide who reaches the local stack (Hosting); `DevSeeder`'s known password makes
    `admin@{{app}}.test` an admin for all of them.
- **Named rate limiters** (`RateLimiter::for`):
<!-- if:htmx -->
  `public` in `AppServiceProvider::boot()`,
<!-- endif -->
  `auth-forms` next to `login`/`two-factor`/`passkeys` in `FortifyServiceProvider`, and `social` beside them once
  social sign-in is built. **Never in `bootstrap/app.php`**: its routing closures do not run under `route:cache`, and
  a route naming a missing limiter answers 500.
- **`Model::shouldBeStrict()`** outside production, so N+1s and silent attribute misses fail loudly.
<!-- if:tenancy -->
- **Tenancy** (root `CLAUDE.md`, Tenancy), all in `AppServiceProvider`:
  - `$this->app->scoped(CurrentTenant::class)`;
  - the `tenantId` and `compileTenantPolicy` macros (`database/CLAUDE.md`);
  - `Context::hydrated(fn (Repository $context) => CurrentTenant::set($context->getHidden('tenant_id')))`
    (`app/Jobs/CLAUDE.md`);
  - `Event::listen(ConnectionEstablished::class, …)`: when the default connection (re)connects while a tenant is
    held, re-run `set_config`. Without it a lost-connection retry runs with no tenant;
  - `Event::listen(Login::class, SelectTenantOnLogin::class)`: writes the default tenant (`ResolveTenant`'s rule)
    into the session; nothing when the user has none, since only the `tenant` middleware answers 403 `no_tenant`.
    `Login` fires for every kind of sign-in, remember-me included;
  - `Sanctum::usePersonalAccessTokenModel(PersonalAccessToken::class)`.

  `/horizon` stays a platform surface: its gate reads the global `users` table and Horizon shows every tenant's
  payloads, so the gate never widens.
<!-- endif -->

## Rules

- **A binding is the Octane leak site**: `scoped()` for anything per request, never a `singleton()` holding request
  or user state (`app/CLAUDE.md`).
- Bindings are **deferred where possible**: the web tier should not build clients holding credentials it does not use
  on that request.
- A new provider goes in `bootstrap/providers.php`, or none of its bindings, observers or policies exist.
- Middleware is registered in `bootstrap/app.php`, not here.
